		<p>First we have the base file that generates us when creating a new project which is called <code>base.html.twig</code> located in <code>nameProject/templates/base.html.twig</code>, we have that the convention that symfony uses, is to end with the extension <strong>.twig</strong> in templates.</p>		

		<p>With twig templates, everything is based on <strong>blocks</strong>, for example we open <strong>block</strong> and we close <strong>endblock</strong> prefixing the percent sign <strong>%</strong> , which can be extended and reused, thereby avoiding unnecessary code repetition.</p>

